Use a nested write on `Guild`: put `update` (or `upsert`) under the `premium` relation field.

```ts
await prisma.guild.update({
  where: { guildId: "123" },
  data: {
    premium: {
      update: { active: true, subtype_monthly: true, expiry: "2026-12-01" },
      // or upsert: { create: {...}, update: {...} } if the PremiumModel may not exist yet
    },
  },
});
```

- **Source:** the "Update a specific related record" section of `apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v7/prisma-client/queries/relation-queries.mdx`. It shows the same nested `update` pattern, but on a one-to-many `posts` relation, where it also takes a `where`. Your `premium` relation is optional one-to-one, so you pass the `data` directly. That adaptation is my reading, not an example from the docs.
- **Other options:** the same file has "Update all related records (or filter)" for nested `updateMany`. Nested `create` is under "Using nested `create`".
- **Not checked:** I didn't look up the one-to-one-specific `upsert` and `update` syntax in `prisma-client-reference.mdx`.

